      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for syncing these properties. One mismatch I noticed: in phosphor-dbus-interfaces, Accelerator BaseSpeedInHz / MaxSpeedInHz / MinSpeedInHz are uint64, but this schema defines them as string. Since this patch is a PDI sync, could we align these property types with PDI?",
      "revId": "856cdfc90ae8886096a1af73e46d30717957f4b9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a004302_b6d16fd9",
        "filename": "schemas/openbmc-dbus.json",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 178,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001712
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T14:45:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we constrain it to be a number we will get a number but that pretty much disables the template var feature.\n\nSo if we do it as you suggested then there will be no way for users to populate these fields from the interface they are probing on.\n\nIf we want to achieve a particular D-Bus type we would have to implement that separately anyways since the schema does not take effect at runtime (it is by default only run in CI).",
      "parentUuid": "81cca728_6d829fa3",
      "revId": "856cdfc90ae8886096a1af73e46d30717957f4b9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
